<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:53:53 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>摄像机捕捉到成年黑猩猩将工具和知识传授给幼崽，向下一代传授重要技能</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cameras-capture-adult-chimpanzees-passing-tools-and-know-how-to-their-young-teaching-important-skills-to-the-next-generation-180989538/</link><description>研究人员录制了塞内加尔野生黑猩猩的视频，向年轻人展示如何用棍子捞出蚂蚁，以及如何用石头砸碎猴面包树果实来打开它，以及其他指导实例</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cameras-capture-adult-chimpanzees-passing-tools-and-know-how-to-their-young-teaching-important-skills-to-the-next-generation-180989538/</guid></item><item><title>工人们从多瑙河中挖出砾石，挖出了一件拥有 2200 年历史的“生锈宝藏”，该宝藏原本可以装备一支军队</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/workers-excavating-gravel-from-the-danube-river-dredged-up-a-2200-year-old-rusty-treasure-that-could-have-equipped-an-army-180989542/</link><description>缓存中至少有 500 根铁条的残骸，这些铁条很可能被送往下游锻造成成品</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/workers-excavating-gravel-from-the-danube-river-dredged-up-a-2200-year-old-rusty-treasure-that-could-have-equipped-an-army-180989542/</guid></item><item><title>一本详细描述特诺奇蒂特兰城兴衰的罕见阿兹特克手抄本近两个世纪以来首次回归墨西哥</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-rare-aztec-codex-detailing-the-rise-and-fall-of-tenochtitlan-returns-to-mexico-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-two-centuries-180989536/</link><description>这件文物是阿兹特克历史上最珍贵的视觉记录之一，将在墨西哥城展出三个月</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:34:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-rare-aztec-codex-detailing-the-rise-and-fall-of-tenochtitlan-returns-to-mexico-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-two-centuries-180989536/</guid></item><item><title>亨利八世在英国宗教改革期间依靠这位朝臣来执行他的命令。在幕后，都铎政治家通过秘密保存天主教文本来反抗他的国王</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/henry-viii-relied-on-this-courtier-to-enforce-his-orders-during-the-english-reformation-behind-the-scenes-the-tudor-politician-defied-his-king-by-secretly-saving-a-catholic-text-180989541/</link><description>一份新发现的碎片表明，约翰·盖奇保存了一份 15 世纪的宗教手稿，“当他打算销毁像这本书一样的书籍时，它保持了安全”</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:08:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/henry-viii-relied-on-this-courtier-to-enforce-his-orders-during-the-english-reformation-behind-the-scenes-the-tudor-politician-defied-his-king-by-secretly-saving-a-catholic-text-180989541/</guid></item><item><title>随着年龄的增长和重大转变，大脑会萎缩。但令人惊讶的是，更年期期间似乎不再需要重新布线</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-brain-shrinks-as-we-age-and-during-major-transitions-but-surprisingly-it-seems-to-take-a-break-from-rewiring-during-menopause-180989527/</link><description>青春期、怀孕和更年期是女性大脑的三个主要荷尔蒙转变。研究人员已经知道，在前两个过程中，器官会根据荷尔蒙的变化进行自我调整，但他们还不确定第三个过程</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:51:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-brain-shrinks-as-we-age-and-during-major-transitions-but-surprisingly-it-seems-to-take-a-break-from-rewiring-during-menopause-180989527/</guid></item><item><title>在俄亥俄州发现的犰狳是装甲动物向北扩张的最新惊喜。他们现在在哪里，是什么推动了他们的行动？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-armadillo-found-in-ohio-is-the-latest-surprise-in-the-armored-animals-expansion-north-where-are-they-now-and-whats-driving-their-movement-180989530/</link><description>这些生物通常出现在南部和东南部，随着冬季变得温和，这些生物已经到达越来越远的州，如北卡罗来纳州、弗吉尼亚州和伊利诺伊州</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:56:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-armadillo-found-in-ohio-is-the-latest-surprise-in-the-armored-animals-expansion-north-where-are-they-now-and-whats-driving-their-movement-180989530/</guid></item><item><title>英国一项尖端举措用镰刀取代割草机，以恢复野花并拯救蜜蜂</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-cutting-edge-english-project-replaces-lawnmowers-with-scythes-to-protect-wildflowers-and-save-the-bees-180989537/</link><description>英国遗产组织招募了志愿者，以传统的方式在一些历史遗址修剪草地</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:46:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-cutting-edge-english-project-replaces-lawnmowers-with-scythes-to-protect-wildflowers-and-save-the-bees-180989537/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，过去 30 年美国与酒精相关的癌症死亡人数增加了一倍多</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/alcohol-related-cancer-deaths-have-more-than-doubled-in-the-united-states-over-the-past-30-years-study-suggests-180989531/</link><description>虽然科学家们表示，他们的发现并不一定意味着您需要完全戒酒，但了解潜在风险（尤其是当您患癌症的风险已经较高时）可以帮助指导您的决定</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:32:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/alcohol-related-cancer-deaths-have-more-than-doubled-in-the-united-states-over-the-past-30-years-study-suggests-180989531/</guid></item><item><title>一位在荷兰图书馆学习的研究人员惊讶地发现了 1,700 年前的《奥德赛》副本中的一小片羊皮纸</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-researcher-studying-in-a-dutch-library-was-amazed-to-discover-a-scrap-of-parchment-from-a-1700-year-old-copy-of-the-odyssey-180989524/</link><description>该手写片段包含荷马史诗第 12 卷中的希腊诗句，其中奥德修斯国王讲述了他注定要灭亡的船员的命运</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-researcher-studying-in-a-dutch-library-was-amazed-to-discover-a-scrap-of-parchment-from-a-1700-year-old-copy-of-the-odyssey-180989524/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下可爱的小蒂尔卡约吧，这是一个多世纪以来第一个被发现的全新猫科动物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-adorable-and-tiny-tilcayo-the-first-brand-new-cat-species-identified-in-more-than-a-century-180989528/</link><description>这种小型猫科动物是在巴西的云林中发现的，它们比家猫还小，全身覆盖着巨大的、不规则形状的玫瑰花结。</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-adorable-and-tiny-tilcayo-the-first-brand-new-cat-species-identified-in-more-than-a-century-180989528/</guid></item><item><title>从“Sunday Scaries”和“Whack-a-Mole”到“Looksmaxxing”和“Cuffing Season”，这些是词典中的最新单词</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-sunday-scaries-and-whack-a-mole-to-looksmaxxing-and-cuffing-season-these-are-the-newest-words-in-the-dictionary-180989529/</link><description>Merriam-Webster 的更新包括 1,400 个已被证明经常、广泛且有意义使用的单词</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:28:11 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-sunday-scaries-and-whack-a-mole-to-looksmaxxing-and-cuffing-season-these-are-the-newest-words-in-the-dictionary-180989529/</guid></item><item><title>月球刚刚出现了一个巨大的新陨石坑，比两个足球场还要宽。这是一次“一生一次的观察”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-moon-just-got-a-massive-new-crater-thats-wider-than-two-end-to-end-football-fields-its-a-once-in-a-lifetime-observation-180989526/</link><description>这个陨石坑形成于 2024 年，当时一个多层建筑大小的物体撞上了我们的月球伴侣。由此产生的草皮大约 728 英尺宽、141 英尺深</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:04:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-moon-just-got-a-massive-new-crater-thats-wider-than-two-end-to-end-football-fields-its-a-once-in-a-lifetime-observation-180989526/</guid></item><item><title>一群 40 个真人大小的野牛木偶将于本周末穿越纽约，以纪念原住民的历史和坚韧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-herd-of-40-life-size-bison-puppets-will-stampede-through-new-york-this-weekend-to-honor-indigenous-history-and-resilience-180989525/</link><description>这些巨大的牛，每头都由三名木偶操纵者操纵，将在曼哈顿下城和布鲁克林漫步</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:44:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-herd-of-40-life-size-bison-puppets-will-stampede-through-new-york-this-weekend-to-honor-indigenous-history-and-resilience-180989525/</guid></item><item><title>几个世纪前，一位建筑师将帕台农神庙的曲线描述为一种巧妙的视错觉。现在，一位数学家提出不同意见</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-an-architect-characterized-the-parthenons-curves-as-a-clever-optical-illusion-now-a-mathematician-begs-to-differ-180989520/</link><description>公元前一世纪，维特鲁威写道，卫城最大的神庙是水平弯曲的，这样它就不会下垂，这种解释持续了数千年。新研究提出了不同的原因</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:11:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-an-architect-characterized-the-parthenons-curves-as-a-clever-optical-illusion-now-a-mathematician-begs-to-differ-180989520/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明霸王龙是一种温血恐龙，体温与人类相似</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tyrannosaurus-rex-was-a-warm-blooded-dinosaur-with-a-body-temperature-similar-to-that-of-humans-study-suggests-180989519/</link><description>牙齿分析表明，这种可怕的掠食者在 97 华氏度的高温下奔跑。维持这种内部温度可能使其能够在白垩纪时期栖息在从现代阿拉斯加到墨西哥的范围内</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:59:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tyrannosaurus-rex-was-a-warm-blooded-dinosaur-with-a-body-temperature-similar-to-that-of-humans-study-suggests-180989519/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员发现，一种致命动物病毒的古老 DNA 已在中世纪手稿中潜伏了几个世纪</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-manuscripts-preserved-traces-of-a-deadly-virus-for-centuries-180989522/</link><description>对牙齿和羊皮纸的一项新分析表明，毁灭性的羊痘病毒已经感染牲畜 3,700 年了</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:10:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-manuscripts-preserved-traces-of-a-deadly-virus-for-centuries-180989522/</guid></item><item><title>座头鲸妈妈一直陪着她死产的小鲸鱼，反复抚摸它并凝视它的眼睛。她悲伤吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-humpback-whale-mom-stayed-with-her-stillborn-calf-repeatedly-touchingi-it-and-staring-into-its-eyes-was-she-grieving-180989516/</link><description>去年在澳大利亚昆士兰州海岸观察到的这一事件标志着该物种死产的首次记录，为了解高度社会性动物如何应对死亡提供了难得的机会</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-humpback-whale-mom-stayed-with-her-stillborn-calf-repeatedly-touchingi-it-and-staring-into-its-eyes-was-she-grieving-180989516/</guid></item><item><title>科学家创造了具有半人脑的老鼠。杂交动物可能会彻底改变我们对神经系统疾病的理解</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-created-mice-with-half-human-brains-the-hybrid-animals-could-revolutionize-our-understanding-of-neurological-disorders-180989518/</link><description>众所周知，我们的大脑及其相关疾病很难研究。因此，研究人员开发了一种动物模型，其皮层（大脑的外层）是由人类细胞生长而来</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 20:16:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-created-mice-with-half-human-brains-the-hybrid-animals-could-revolutionize-our-understanding-of-neurological-disorders-180989518/</guid></item><item><title>教皇利奥十四世在梵蒂冈图书馆举办以水为主题的艺术展，庆祝他的 71 岁生日，引起轰动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/pope-leo-xiv-makes-a-splash-for-his-71st-birthday-announcing-a-water-themed-art-exhibition-at-the-vatican-library-180989515/</link><description>当代雕塑、由印刷元素制成的鱼、具有数百年历史的论文和历史性的全球烹饪书将在新的“灾难与奇迹”艺术展中亮相</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:12:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/pope-leo-xiv-makes-a-splash-for-his-71st-birthday-announcing-a-water-themed-art-exhibition-at-the-vatican-library-180989515/</guid></item><item><title>这幅失传已久的格特鲁德·阿伯克龙比 (Gertrude Abercrombie) 画作在一次房地产拍卖会上以 30 美元的价格买下，现在可以卖到 25 万美元</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/bought-for-30-at-an-estate-sale-this-long-lost-gertrude-abercrombie-painting-could-now-fetch-250000-180989513/</link><description>这位来自芝加哥的超现实主义者于 1951 年创作了这件作品，然后将其送给了一位医生以换取医疗服务</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:02:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/bought-for-30-at-an-estate-sale-this-long-lost-gertrude-abercrombie-painting-could-now-fetch-250000-180989513/</guid></item></channel></rss>